37
00:02:03,648 --> 00:02:07,848
Okay, aggressive buyers. Aggressive buyers are buyers who buy from the offer.

38
00:02:08,148 --> 00:02:11,348
The market will be bid and offered all the time.

39
00:02:12,548 --> 00:02:17,248
An aggressive buyer is someone that buys the offer. So, for example...

40
00:02:19,448 --> 00:02:25,248
At this price, 1908, the market is 1908 bid offered at 1908 and a quarter.

41
00:02:27,348 --> 00:02:28,848
So the market is trading back and forth.

42
00:02:29,048 --> 00:02:35,148
Whoever is buying the 1908s in the quarter, those are considered the aggressive buyers.

43
00:02:36,048 --> 00:02:40,148
If someone was selling into the 1908 bid, you'd consider that aggressive sellers.

44
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:48,320
So the next one is aggressive sellers. The sellers who sell into the bid.

45
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:50,520
So as I was saying

46
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:53,180
before, people that are selling into this

47
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:57,360
1908 bid, these 49 lots that traded here, those are the aggressive sellers.

48
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:04,120
Delta, ask Delta.

49
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:11,320
The total amount of volume traded on the offer in a bar, the amount bought by aggressive buyers.

50
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:13,256
So you have down

51
00:03:13,256 --> 00:03:15,710
here, you can see on some

52
00:03:15,710 --> 00:03:20,619
charts, on some software, they'll show you what the ask delta is.

53
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:25,820
And what the bid delta is, the delta, the max delta. There's a lot of different types of deltas.

54
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,620
One of them is the ask delta.

55
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:35,120
And what it is, it's the volume that's traded on the offer, what was bought from the offer.

56
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:39,520
When the market was 1915 at 1915 and a quarter,

57
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:44,120
1,666 lots traded on the offer.

58
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:51,820
So you take the volume that's traded on the ask side versus what's traded on the bid side.

59
00:03:53,220 --> 00:04:00,320
you'll get the delta, but all the volume that's traded on the ask side, that is the ask delta.

60
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:05,320
If you were to add up all these numbers here, you'd get 17,831.

61
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:10,420
Mid-delta is opposite of

62
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:13,198
the ask delta again

63
00:04:13,198 --> 00:04:14,545
it'll show up down here

64
00:04:14,545 --> 00:04:18,318
with your delta numbers it's all the volume that's traded on the bid side

65
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:28,520
Okay, an average ratio number, aka a normal ratio number.

66
00:04:29,820 --> 00:04:36,120
Now, OrderFlows Trader is the only software that has ratios.

67
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:40,120
So if you're not using OrderFlows Trader, this really won't make much sense to you.

68
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:43,100
But a ratio number that is black color as opposed

69
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:45,718
to a blue number indicates that the ratio is just normal.

70
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:49,320
A regular ratio without price rejection or absorption.

71
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:55,220
You're going to see two types of numbers on the top of a bar or below a bar.

72
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:56,920
If it's a red bar, it'll be on top.

73
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:59,920
If it's a green bar, it'll be on the bottom.

74
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:02,336
So in this case, you have a

75
00:05:02,336 --> 00:05:04,552
black number here. You have a blue

76
00:05:04,552 --> 00:05:07,717
number here. The black number is an average ratio number.

77
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:12,720
It's one that doesn't meet the requirements of indicating that there is

78
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:18,820
a lack of follow through on a move or price rejection.

79
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:24,320
Here you have a 90.5, here you have 2.067.

80
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:30,520
I'll get into it later what the ratios mean, but for now we'll just talk about the colors.

81
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:32,520
An average ratio number is going to be black.

82
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:40,620
A ratio that's in blue will indicate something, like either strong offers,

83
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:45,320
strong bids or lack of buying or lack of selling.

84
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:49,720
Next one is a buying imbalance.

85
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,277
A buying imbalance occurs when

86
00:05:51,277 --> 00:05:57,506
buyers are aggressively buying from the offer at a ratio of 400% or greater relative to what's sold on the bid.

87
00:05:58,220 --> 00:06:01,620
So down here you have this buying imbalance.

88
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,420
You have 49 against 263.

89
00:06:05,820 --> 00:06:10,420
The 263 is in blue indicating a buying imbalance.

90
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:15,220
You take in the ratio of 49 against 263, it's over 400%.

91
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:19,020
That's why it's showing up as a buying imbalance.

92
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:22,720
Here you have 134 against 358.

93
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:29,720
It's not a buying imbalance because 134 into 358 is less than 400%.

94
00:06:34,224 --> 00:06:40,524
The commitment of traders in order flows context, it is the price in a bar where the most volume occurs.

95
00:06:41,624 --> 00:06:48,324
So on most order flow software, they'll put a box around the commitment of traders.

96
00:06:48,524 --> 00:06:50,824
It's also called point of control.

97
00:06:50,824 --> 00:06:55,724
You hear the term POC, COT, point of control, commitment of traders.

98
00:06:56,324 --> 00:06:59,424
In order flow context, on a footprint chart, they all have the same meaning.

99
00:07:00,424 --> 00:07:04,924
Some people like to refer to it as COT, others like to refer to it as point of control.

100
00:07:06,024 --> 00:07:10,824
And what it's telling you is where in the bar the most volume appeared.

101
00:07:11,224 --> 00:07:17,424
So you see here, you got 4614 and 4414. It just takes the price level.

102
00:07:17,524 --> 00:07:21,724
It's not measuring it diagonally, what traded against the bid, what's traded on the offer.

103
00:07:21,824 --> 00:07:24,924
It's taking the price level where the most volume occurred.

104
00:07:27,328 --> 00:07:31,728
Cumulative delta is the accumulation of delta over the entire trading session.

105
00:07:32,228 --> 00:07:34,028
You'll see down here, cumulative delta.

106
00:07:35,428 --> 00:07:44,028
So each bar will have a delta of either 0, which is rare, or a positive or negative number.

107
00:07:44,228 --> 00:07:48,128
And it's taking the cumulative number since the beginning of the session.

108
00:07:48,428 --> 00:07:54,328
So say it's a session that's been rallying. Generally, you'll have a positive cumulative delta.

109
00:07:54,428 --> 00:07:59,285
If you're in a session that's been selling off all day long,

110
00:07:59,285 --> 00:08:02,927
most often you should have a negative cumulative delta.

111
00:08:05,344 --> 00:08:09,344
Cumulative volume is the accumulation of volume over the entire trading session.

112
00:08:09,844 --> 00:08:11,444
It's going to be on the bottom here.

113
00:08:11,944 --> 00:08:15,220
With NinjaTrader, they put their copyright logo right

114
00:08:15,220 --> 00:08:20,543
over that, so you can't really see it, or at least the label.

115
00:08:20,644 --> 00:08:24,744
You can see the numbers, but you can't see that it says cumulative volume.

116
00:08:24,944 --> 00:08:26,644
And what that is, it's the day's volume.

117
00:08:27,244 --> 00:08:28,144
Why is that important?

118
00:08:29,544 --> 00:08:35,744
You can judge if the market is fast or slow, I mean busy or not, by the cumulative delta.

119
00:08:36,044 --> 00:08:39,944
You know, by certain times of day, you should have reached a certain amount of volume.

120
00:08:40,944 --> 00:08:45,144
On slow days or holidays, you'll notice that the volume is much lighter.

121
00:08:46,644 --> 00:08:48,644
And you can see that in the cumulative volume.

122
00:08:48,644 --> 00:08:55,444
Like you say, by 9.30, you should already have half a million contracts in the E-minis have traded.

123
00:08:55,844 --> 00:08:58,344
If it's much less, then the volume is light.

124
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:01,391
The delta.

125
00:09:01,391 --> 00:09:04,348
The delta is the difference in a bar between the

126
00:09:04,348 --> 00:09:07,897
volume traded on the offer minus the volume traded on the bid.

127
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:13,500
Now, you see also later positive delta and negative delta in the definitions.

128
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:16,300
And delta is very important.

129
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,600
It's something that not a lot of people...

130
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:20,700
Look at at all.

131
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:26,000
Basically only order flow traders really spend any time with delta.

132
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:28,400
And you know why is it important?

133
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:35,500
On bars that are up, you know bars that open and then close higher.

134
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,595
You know if a bar opens

135
00:09:37,595 --> 00:09:38,924
down here at 1915 and a

136
00:09:38,924 --> 00:09:41,583
quarter, closes at 1917 and a quarter, it's an up bar.

137
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:44,700
It should have positive delta.

138
00:09:47,596 --> 00:09:56,096
So you're taking what's traded, the ask delta minus the bid delta to get the total delta for the bar.

139
00:09:56,796 --> 00:10:02,896
So in an up move, you know, when a market's rallying, you should string together positive deltas in each bar.

140
00:10:03,296 --> 00:10:08,496
There will be bars that are, you know, red bars, negative bars that do have a positive delta.

141
00:10:08,896 --> 00:10:12,996
And there will be green bars that do have... Negative delta.

142
00:10:13,896 --> 00:10:16,696
Delta is a function of the volume that's traded inside the bar.

143
00:10:17,896 --> 00:10:19,010
It's important, you

144
00:10:19,010 --> 00:10:25,695
know, I'll explain later, I have a whole chapter, a whole lesson developed around delta and its importance.

145
00:10:26,296 --> 00:10:31,296
But in general, on a move up, you should be having positive deltas.

146
00:10:32,096 --> 00:10:34,796
And on a move down, you should be having negative deltas.

147
00:10:37,116 --> 00:10:38,681
Divergence, in order flow terms,

148
00:10:38,681 --> 00:10:40,873
is when a market makes a new

149
00:10:40,873 --> 00:10:43,378
or equal high and the bar has a

150
00:10:43,378 --> 00:10:49,014
negative delta, or when a market makes a new or equal low and the bar has positive delta.

151
00:10:49,116 --> 00:10:55,316
Basically, price is acting different than an indicator. In this case, the indicator is the delta.

152
00:10:55,616 --> 00:11:00,616
So if you're making a high and you have negative delta, technically that's a divergence.

153
00:11:05,416 --> 00:11:08,316
People also refer to it as delta divergence.

154
00:11:08,616 --> 00:11:10,494
It's usually marked with a triangle

155
00:11:10,494 --> 00:11:12,372
on a chart. I mean, most

156
00:11:12,372 --> 00:11:15,815
are, depending on some charts. Some charts don't even show it.

157
00:11:16,216 --> 00:11:17,016
Why is that important?

158
00:11:17,116 --> 00:11:19,116
Well, you hit the high.

159
00:11:20,716 --> 00:11:24,816
And there's a lot of selling in there causing a negative delta, that's important to know.

160
00:11:25,016 --> 00:11:27,516
You're not going to necessarily see that on just a normal bar chart.

161
00:11:28,016 --> 00:11:29,067
So if you can

162
00:11:29,067 --> 00:11:30,380
see, you know, markets rallying,

163
00:11:30,380 --> 00:11:31,956
rallying, rallying, then you hit the

164
00:11:31,956 --> 00:11:33,795
high, and all of a sudden sellers

165
00:11:33,795 --> 00:11:35,371
come in and overwhelm the buyers,

166
00:11:35,371 --> 00:11:39,311
and you've got a big negative delta like you have here, the market should react.

167
00:11:40,316 --> 00:11:45,351
Now, in a market that keeps rallying all day, you will get more and more deltas, you

168
00:11:45,351 --> 00:11:50,816
know, just as maybe the market starts to pull back. You should take everything into context.

169
00:11:51,516 --> 00:11:56,816
I get into a little bit more with reversal signals later in the course.

170
00:11:58,716 --> 00:12:01,616
Footprint chart, this is a chart used by Order Flows Trader.

171
00:12:02,316 --> 00:12:05,016
Footprint chart is the generic term that's

172
00:12:06,116 --> 00:12:11,516
most order flow software uses to break down the volume traded on the bid and the offer.

173
00:12:15,716 --> 00:12:19,616
It provides the price, the bid traded volume, and the offer traded volume together.

174
00:12:20,016 --> 00:12:22,448
So you can see what traded on

175
00:12:22,448 --> 00:12:24,880
the bid, what traded on the offer,

176
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:27,312
and how it compares with each other.

177
00:12:27,316 --> 00:12:35,016
And as the market's moving, it's called a footprint chart because imagine an animal walking through.

178
00:12:35,716 --> 00:12:36,316
The mud, right?

179
00:12:36,316 --> 00:12:39,416
It leaves a footprint just as traders are trading through the market.

180
00:12:39,416 --> 00:12:43,816
They're leaving their footprint in the market as measured by volume.

181
00:12:45,516 --> 00:12:46,244
So imbalance on

182
00:12:46,244 --> 00:12:47,943
a high. Imbalance on a high occurs

183
00:12:47,943 --> 00:12:50,613
when there's a buy and imbalance on top of red bar.

184
00:12:51,616 --> 00:12:56,116
What this means is it's a sell signal. You want to trade in the opposite direction.

185
00:12:56,516 --> 00:12:58,916
Some people will call it trap traders.

186
00:12:59,716 --> 00:13:02,016
I don't particularly like to use that term, trap traders.

187
00:13:02,916 --> 00:13:07,716
Just because most markets are pretty liquid that, you know, these guys, they're trapped.

188
00:13:08,216 --> 00:13:09,716
They can get out pretty easily.

189
00:13:10,916 --> 00:13:13,816
But why is it important is imbalance on a high.

190
00:13:14,516 --> 00:13:17,716
Here you have the blue number, which is indicating a buying imbalance.

191
00:13:17,716 --> 00:13:19,916
So you got 221 against 1045.

192
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:24,516
So it's a ratio of, you know, 400% more that's traded on the offer.

193
00:13:24,916 --> 00:13:27,216
But why didn't the market rally keep going?

194
00:13:27,216 --> 00:13:29,064
You have a lot of aggressive

195
00:13:29,064 --> 00:13:34,916
buyers, people trying to buy the breakout. But they can't push it any further. It just stops right there.

196
00:13:36,916 --> 00:13:40,316
You want to take it in context with where the market is.

197
00:13:40,816 --> 00:13:45,916
If it's just an imbalance on the top of a red bar and the market going sideways, is it important?

198
00:13:46,316 --> 00:13:51,216
Yes, probably, but it's more powerful when it's at the end of a move.

199
00:13:51,916 --> 00:13:55,316
Rather than just sort of stuck in the middle of a move on a market that's going nowhere.

200
00:13:56,316 --> 00:14:00,472
I always say you can have the greatest indicator in the world,

201
00:14:00,472 --> 00:14:03,242
but if it shoots off a perfect signal

202
00:14:03,242 --> 00:14:06,012
right in the middle of a trading range

203
00:14:06,012 --> 00:14:10,514
where the market's going nowhere, it's not going to be very lucrative trading.

204
00:14:14,036 --> 00:14:19,036
So the next one would be an imbalance on the low, which is opposite to the imbalance on a high.

205
00:14:19,136 --> 00:14:21,936
It occurs when there's a selling imbalance at the bottom of a green bar.

206
00:14:22,736 --> 00:14:24,112
And what you want to do is you

207
00:14:24,112 --> 00:14:25,316
want to trade in the opposite direction.

208
00:14:25,316 --> 00:14:27,036
So in this case, it would be a buy signal.

209
00:14:28,336 --> 00:14:32,436
So you see here, you've got 1068 right on the low. It's a selling imbalance.

210
00:14:34,036 --> 00:14:36,336
People are being aggressive. They're selling it into the bid.

211
00:14:36,736 --> 00:14:39,036
Why isn't the market selling off more?

212
00:14:40,036 --> 00:14:41,213
Obviously, there was

213
00:14:41,213 --> 00:14:43,175
somebody in there with a

214
00:14:43,175 --> 00:14:45,923
strong bid, a strong passive bid to

215
00:14:45,923 --> 00:14:50,634
support the market that basically they're saying, I'll take all you got.

216
00:14:51,636 --> 00:14:55,336
They're not going to let the market go through that level. They may be defending the level.

217
00:14:56,136 --> 00:14:58,436
Now, imbalances on highs and lows.

218
00:15:00,236 --> 00:15:06,636
Are not going to be the end of trend or the high or the low of the day.

219
00:15:07,136 --> 00:15:08,536
They happen in the course of trading.

220
00:15:08,936 --> 00:15:14,136
The market may come back to those levels later and test it and get through those levels.

221
00:15:14,236 --> 00:15:18,936
You don't necessarily know if those participants are still there when the market circles around back to those levels.

222
00:15:19,036 --> 00:15:26,436
But for the short term, it's a nice little indicator to add to your cap, especially

223
00:15:27,136 --> 00:15:30,136
when you're, you know, you've got to think about what's happening to the market.

224
00:15:30,136 --> 00:15:34,836
So you have the market coming down. You have some very aggressive sellers right at the low.

225
00:15:34,936 --> 00:15:40,336
The market turns around. Market price action in the bar shows that there's buyers in there.

226
00:15:40,836 --> 00:15:44,536
In this case, in this example, you've got a buying imbalance at the top end of the bar.

227
00:15:45,236 --> 00:15:49,336
So, you know, these people that sold earlier, you know, they're stuck.

228
00:15:49,336 --> 00:15:50,236
They got to get out.

229
00:15:50,336 --> 00:15:53,736
You know, if they want to get out, they're going to add to the buying.

230
00:15:54,036 --> 00:15:59,736
But what's important is the buying couldn't follow through and... And that's where it turned.

231
00:16:00,036 --> 00:16:05,436
It turned because there was some decent stopping volume there in the market to absorb all the aggressive sellers.

232
00:16:11,036 --> 00:16:17,436
Okay, imbalance trigger in percent. It's the percentage used in determining if there is a binary selling imbalance.

233
00:16:17,436 --> 00:16:19,736
The common accepted level is 400 as a minimum.

234
00:16:20,536 --> 00:16:23,536
Um, Some people I know use 350.

235
00:16:23,836 --> 00:16:25,436
Some people I know use 1,000.

236
00:16:27,336 --> 00:16:29,036
400% is a good starting point.

237
00:16:29,236 --> 00:16:37,836
Whether you want to be more selective or let a few more imbalances in, it's up to you.

238
00:16:39,036 --> 00:16:43,336
But most softwares will allow you to adjust the imbalance trigger percent.

239
00:16:47,792 --> 00:16:49,592
Imbalance volume threshold.

240
00:16:49,792 --> 00:16:51,587
Okay, now this is one that's unique

241
00:16:51,587 --> 00:16:53,382
to the order flows trader. You're only

242
00:16:53,382 --> 00:16:55,689
going to get it with the order flows trader.

243
00:16:55,792 --> 00:17:00,492
And what it is, it's the minimum traded volume on the bid or offer when there's an imbalance.

244
00:17:00,992 --> 00:17:03,143
It's important if you don't want to see

245
00:17:03,143 --> 00:17:05,294
imbalances where volume involved is less than a

246
00:17:05,294 --> 00:17:06,638
certain amount, for example, 10 lots.

247
00:17:07,692 --> 00:17:09,692
Setting it to a bigger number will show imbalances.

248
00:17:11,592 --> 00:17:15,092
When more volume is in the imbalance.

249
00:17:17,668 --> 00:17:22,168
when it's taking more volume to move the market.

250
00:17:22,368 --> 00:17:23,668
I have it set at 50.

251
00:17:25,568 --> 00:17:28,468
And I use that pretty much for all markets as the minimum.

252
00:17:28,468 --> 00:17:35,168
I don't want to see an imbalance of 1 against 6 or 2 against 8.

253
00:17:35,568 --> 00:17:39,968
To me, technically those are imbalances because the ratio is greater than 400%.

254
00:17:40,368 --> 00:17:44,368
But if you're trading thinner markets that...

255
00:17:45,168 --> 00:17:47,168
Sometimes you're going to

256
00:17:47,168 --> 00:17:50,168
get these markets, for example, some

257
00:17:50,168 --> 00:17:57,668
of the green markets, even to a lesser extent, like NQ, NASDAQ, mini-DAO, DAX even.

258
00:17:57,668 --> 00:18:02,868
You're going to get these bars that are moving around very fast, and you're getting ratios of 1 against 5.

259
00:18:03,168 --> 00:18:09,468
Technically, that is an imbalance, but it's an imbalance that's not necessarily occurring on very much volume.

260
00:18:10,368 --> 00:18:16,968
I like to see it when it matters, and when it matters is when there's decent volume that's traded.

261
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:23,060
Okay, a large print on the bottom.Now,

262
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:26,902
It's similar in the sense to

263
00:18:26,902 --> 00:18:28,644
an imbalance on the higher, the

264
00:18:28,644 --> 00:18:31,258
lower, only in this case it's a large print.

265
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,360
It's not a...

266
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:37,360
It's not an imbalance.

267
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:40,760
It's just a very big stopping volume there.

268
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:47,160
And what it indicates is there's heavy volume at the bottom of the bar.

269
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:49,960
So I refer to it as stopping volume.

270
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:52,360
It occurs at the bottom of a green candlestick.

271
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:56,860
When there's heavy volume traded at the extreme bottom of the bar, right here.

272
00:18:57,860 --> 00:18:59,896
Now it's most effective at swing lows or

273
00:18:59,896 --> 00:19:01,677
lows of the day, but it can

274
00:19:01,677 --> 00:19:03,458
occur in the middle of a move.

275
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:06,430
And if it does, you could

276
00:19:06,430 --> 00:19:08,200
use it as as a level

277
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:10,856
to trade around if you're already in the move.

278
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:11,579
You know, you

279
00:19:11,579 --> 00:19:12,610
could, if you like to

280
00:19:12,610 --> 00:19:13,848
try your stop, you know, you

281
00:19:13,848 --> 00:19:14,879
have this volume here, you

282
00:19:14,879 --> 00:19:17,355
can sort of hide behind, you know, as the market goes up.

283
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:20,312
You know, if it's going to pull back, you can look to see how it reacts

284
00:19:20,312 --> 00:19:22,158
around there to decide if you're going to get out.

285
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:24,959
But, like I said, it's most

286
00:19:24,959 --> 00:19:26,558
effective, I feel, when it's at

287
00:19:26,558 --> 00:19:29,757
the lows of the day or at a low of a move.

288
00:19:31,160 --> 00:19:33,360
It's basically someone coming in and supporting the market.

289
00:19:37,708 --> 00:19:39,108
Okay, a large print on the top.

290
00:19:40,608 --> 00:19:42,008
It's referred to as stopping volume.

291
00:19:42,008 --> 00:19:47,308
It's basically the mirror image of large print on the bottom, only this time it's at the top.

292
00:19:48,308 --> 00:19:49,983
It'll occur at the top of a red

293
00:19:49,983 --> 00:19:52,706
candlestick where there's heavy volume traded at the extreme top of the bar.

294
00:19:53,308 --> 00:19:57,108
Most effective at swing lows of the day, but can occur in a move.

295
00:20:00,208 --> 00:20:03,008
The order flows trader software will give a ratio.

296
00:20:03,408 --> 00:20:05,698
That's why you see a blue number

297
00:20:05,698 --> 00:20:07,988
here, which is indicating that there is

298
00:20:07,988 --> 00:20:10,605
the volume at the top of the candlestick.

299
00:20:11,408 --> 00:20:15,008
If it was on a bottom, it would appear at the bottom.

300
00:20:15,308 --> 00:20:17,146
I'll get into the ratios a

301
00:20:17,146 --> 00:20:19,597
little bit later, but what's important to know

302
00:20:19,597 --> 00:20:21,435
is the large print on the

303
00:20:21,435 --> 00:20:24,805
top is oftentimes the beginning of the end of a move.

304
00:20:28,532 --> 00:20:35,432
The max delta, it indicates that the maximum delta exhibited in a bar at any point.

305
00:20:35,432 --> 00:20:39,932
So when you have a max delta, so you can see this candlestick here.

306
00:20:40,432 --> 00:20:44,132
The delta for the bar, it ended up at 1,630.

307
00:20:44,732 --> 00:20:52,732
The max delta, which was the most positive delta, in the bar was 2,630.

308
00:20:53,332 --> 00:20:59,132
So somewhere in there, it lost 1,000 lots of delta.

309
00:20:59,432 --> 00:21:01,032
So obviously there was some selling in there.

310
00:21:01,032 --> 00:21:11,532
I mean, it was very strong, got up to 2,630, but there was some selling, and it ended up just at 1,630.

311
00:21:14,348 --> 00:21:20,248
In this next bar, this one here at 1141, you can see the max delta is 1778.

312
00:21:22,148 --> 00:21:29,148
The delta for the bar closed at 1773. The minimum delta was minus 1,644.

313
00:21:29,148 --> 00:21:35,148
So at one point in the bar, it had a delta of minus 1,644.

314
00:21:36,148 --> 00:21:42,448
Obviously, buying came in and you had a positive delta of 1,778.

315
00:21:42,448 --> 00:21:47,848
The bar closed with a... Net delta of 1,733.

316
00:21:50,448 --> 00:21:53,848
Max delta, min deltas are kind of important.

317
00:21:54,048 --> 00:21:57,204
I think when the numbers are zero, either the max

318
00:21:57,204 --> 00:22:00,044
or the min, or when you see big shifts

319
00:22:00,044 --> 00:22:04,147
in delta when a bar was extremely negative, then it turns extremely positive.

320
00:22:08,060 --> 00:22:12,360
So the min delta sort of works the opposite way as maximum delta.

321
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:18,960
It's the most negative delta in the bar during that bar.

322
00:22:19,260 --> 00:22:23,960
So this bar at 1125, it has a min delta of minus 0.

323
00:22:25,460 --> 00:22:29,560
There was never a net negative delta since the bar started.

324
00:22:29,660 --> 00:22:35,760
It was always positive, even though, I mean, there is obviously volume traded into the bid side.

325
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:46,660
But it wasn't enough to turn the delta, this number here, 1630, at any point to minus 100 or anything like that.

326
00:22:47,060 --> 00:22:49,360
It was always on the positive side in the bar.

327
00:22:49,860 --> 00:22:54,860
So you see in this next bar, it has a min delta of minus 1644.

328
00:22:55,260 --> 00:23:01,060
It has a maximum delta of 1778. And the delta closed at 1733.

329
00:23:01,460 --> 00:23:09,423
So at one point in the bar, it did have a negative

330
00:23:09,423 --> 00:23:15,395
delta of minus 1644 as its total highest negative delta.

331
00:23:17,460 --> 00:23:21,460
Obviously, buying came back later in the bar and turned

332
00:23:21,460 --> 00:23:24,660
the delta positive and it went from minus

333
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:27,060
1644 to zero to positive and it

334
00:23:28,260 --> 00:23:33,960
traded all the way up to having a positive delta of 1778 and it ended at 1733.

335
00:23:39,116 --> 00:23:45,316
Negative delta indicates that more volume was sold into the bid. In other words, aggressive sellers were stronger than buyers.

336
00:23:45,416 --> 00:23:50,616
So, you know, the delta, you're going to look at the delta number on a bar.

337
00:23:50,816 --> 00:23:57,616
And if it's positive, then it's positive delta. If it's negative, then it's considered negative delta.

338
00:23:58,216 --> 00:23:59,216
Why is it important?

339
00:23:59,216 --> 00:24:04,124
It's important when the market is moving up or down and you're stringing together negative

340
00:24:04,124 --> 00:24:06,414
deltas, the market should be moving lower.

341
00:24:06,916 --> 00:24:10,554
If you're up near the highs and you're starting to string together

342
00:24:10,554 --> 00:24:12,676
negative deltas and the market's not going

343
00:24:12,676 --> 00:24:16,314
anywhere, either the market has a propensity to later sell off or...

344
00:24:16,716 --> 00:24:21,516
You know, go sideways for a while until selling sort of subsided.

345
00:24:22,016 --> 00:24:26,216
But, I mean, we'll get into the analysis of delta, you know, later.

346
00:24:26,716 --> 00:24:28,541
But what's, you know, just understand

347
00:24:28,541 --> 00:24:30,366
when a bar has a delta

348
00:24:30,366 --> 00:24:31,886
number that's negative, that's negative

349
00:24:31,886 --> 00:24:34,015
delta. If it's positive, that's positive delta.

350
00:24:35,516 --> 00:24:40,716
So... A normal ratio number, aka average ratio number.

351
00:24:41,716 --> 00:24:44,257
I discussed it in under average ratio number earlier, but

352
00:24:44,257 --> 00:24:46,036
it's a ratio number that is black

353
00:24:46,036 --> 00:24:47,815
color as opposed to a blue color.

354
00:24:48,216 --> 00:24:49,816
In any case, that's ratio is just normal.

355
00:24:52,016 --> 00:24:54,416
It's regular ratio without price rejection or absorption.

356
00:24:54,416 --> 00:24:59,216
It's just a number that you know, you expect to see in the market, right?

357
00:24:59,416 --> 00:25:05,516
The markets, you know, exist to facilitate trade. And, you know, that's... That's what they're there for.

358
00:25:05,516 --> 00:25:10,716
So most of the times you're going to have average or normal ratio numbers.

359
00:25:10,816 --> 00:25:16,316
It's when you're going to get ratio numbers that are blue that something's happening in the market.

360
00:25:16,916 --> 00:25:20,169
So like in this case here, even though

361
00:25:20,169 --> 00:25:23,422
you have a buying imbalance on the top,

362
00:25:23,422 --> 00:25:29,115
the numbers, the volumes that are involved around this top, they're just average numbers.

363
00:25:29,616 --> 00:25:32,916
The one thing that stands out, though, is you have the buying imbalance at the top.

364
00:25:33,216 --> 00:25:34,449
I mean, it would be

365
00:25:34,449 --> 00:25:35,682
nice if it was also...

366
00:25:35,682 --> 00:25:36,915
You know, the volume involved

367
00:25:36,915 --> 00:25:38,148
would kick off a ratio,

368
00:25:38,148 --> 00:25:40,614
but, you know, it does sometimes and sometimes it doesn't.

369
00:25:41,116 --> 00:25:45,116
Just like here, you have a single print, but you don't necessarily have the ratio.

370
00:25:48,420 --> 00:25:52,720
But, you know, I'll get into an explanation of the ratios a bit later.

371
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:55,900
So opposing bars, this

372
00:25:55,900 --> 00:25:58,260
is a term that I use often in

373
00:25:58,260 --> 00:26:00,916
the trading room, it's when two side-by-side bars

374
00:26:00,916 --> 00:26:02,391
are opposite in direction, a

375
00:26:02,391 --> 00:26:03,866
green candle followed by a

376
00:26:03,866 --> 00:26:06,919
red candle, or a red candle followed by a green candle.

377
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:09,920
Usually you've got the point of controls at the same levels.

378
00:26:11,220 --> 00:26:12,620
Like here, you've got...

379
00:26:13,320 --> 00:26:15,336
You know, you got a red bar,

380
00:26:15,336 --> 00:26:17,352
you got a green bar following it,

381
00:26:17,352 --> 00:26:20,520
and you got point of controls right at the same level.

382
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:24,920
And we can tell that you got green, red, green, red, green.

383
00:26:26,120 --> 00:26:28,657
Once you start stringing together bars like that,

384
00:26:28,657 --> 00:26:31,194
especially when the point of controls are kind

385
00:26:31,194 --> 00:26:33,731
of, you know, the same level, Oftentimes, it's

386
00:26:33,731 --> 00:26:37,219
an indication of a market that's going nowhere, is trading sideways.

387
00:26:39,520 --> 00:26:41,128
I mean, you know, people can

388
00:26:41,128 --> 00:26:42,736
read into it a little bit

389
00:26:42,736 --> 00:26:46,220
more with the point of controls as being the support or resistance levels.

390
00:26:46,620 --> 00:26:48,615
But for me, I just find that

391
00:26:48,615 --> 00:26:50,610
when I start seeing opposing bars lined

392
00:26:50,610 --> 00:26:54,316
up in a row, it's usually a market that's going to go sideways.

393
00:26:57,300 --> 00:27:03,200
Passive buyers are buyers who get filled while working a bid.

394
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:08,500
So there's two types of buyers. There's aggressive buyers and there's passive buyers.

395
00:27:09,100 --> 00:27:12,118
So passive buyer is somebody that is working

396
00:27:12,118 --> 00:27:15,136
a limit order, whereas an aggressive buyer is

397
00:27:15,136 --> 00:27:17,399
someone who buys at the market.

398
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:23,900
Imagine that you are trying to buy a car or trying to buy a house.

399
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:27,400
You have a price you want to pay and you don't want to budge from that.

400
00:27:27,400 --> 00:27:28,800
You're considered a passive buyer.

401
00:27:29,100 --> 00:27:34,500
You're waiting for that person to come down and meet you at your price. You're waiting for the aggressive seller.

402
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:38,900
Passive buyers... Are at every price level.

403
00:27:39,900 --> 00:27:43,800
When you see big passive buying in the market, you should pay attention to it.

404
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:50,600
Numbers that really stick out quite strongly. Sometimes they're more obvious than not.

405
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:54,900
But in a bar, you're going to get passive buyers, you're going to get passive sellers.

406
00:27:57,400 --> 00:28:02,126
When you're reading the order flow, you want to read what's sort of happening around the edges of the bars.

407
00:28:02,126 --> 00:28:05,198
Oftentimes, we'll give you clues as to what's going on in the market.

408
00:28:06,900 --> 00:28:08,400
So passive sellers, again, it's

409
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:10,500
opposite of what passive buyers are. These

410
00:28:10,500 --> 00:28:13,200
are sellers who get filled while working an offer.

411
00:28:13,600 --> 00:28:21,500
So, you know, say the market's $18.88 and three-quarters bid offered at $18.89.

412
00:28:22,100 --> 00:28:24,800
The people that are trying to sell it at $18.89,

413
00:28:24,900 --> 00:28:26,000
are the passive sellers.

414
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:29,900
They're happy to sit there and wait for people to buy it at their price.

415
00:28:35,800 --> 00:28:43,300
So the point of control, again, it's oftentimes referred to as commitment of traders or COT.

416
00:28:44,400 --> 00:28:46,179
In order for context, it is the

417
00:28:46,179 --> 00:28:47,958
price of the bar where the most

418
00:28:47,958 --> 00:28:50,499
volume occurs. It's going to have the box around it.

419
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:57,200
Positive delta indicates that more volume

420
00:28:57,200 --> 00:28:59,600
was bought from the offer. In other words,

421
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:01,700
aggressive buyers were stronger than aggressive sellers.

422
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:04,773
So if you have a bar with positive

423
00:29:04,773 --> 00:29:08,239
delta, it means net-net there was more volume traded on

424
00:29:08,239 --> 00:29:12,399
the offer, people buying the offer than people selling into the bid.

425
00:29:13,400 --> 00:29:17,900
Again, When the market's moving up, you expect to see positive delta.

426
00:29:18,600 --> 00:29:21,800
On a market that's moving down, you expect to see negative delta.

427
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:24,500
No, that's not always the case.

428
00:29:24,900 --> 00:29:33,600
There's times where you have a market that's sort of going sideways and you have positive deltas and negative deltas.

429
00:29:34,100 --> 00:29:42,800
And nobody's really in control, but Delta is really very fascinating, I think.

430
00:29:43,900 --> 00:29:46,557
I think it's really, as far

431
00:29:46,557 --> 00:29:53,199
as analysis goes, can really tell you a lot about what's happening in the market.

432
00:29:55,700 --> 00:29:56,700
Ratio bounds high.

433
00:29:57,200 --> 00:30:04,100
Okay, again, this is something that only order flows trader software has.

434
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:09,800
And it's the ratio I use to determine if there's a small print occurring in a bar.

435
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:11,946
I set my ratio bounds high at 28 because I

436
00:30:11,946 --> 00:30:13,676
want to be notified when there's a ratio

437
00:30:13,676 --> 00:30:16,704
above 28, which will indicate there's a small print at the edge of the bar.

438
00:30:18,700 --> 00:30:20,500
I refer to this as small print or single print.

439
00:30:20,600 --> 00:30:24,000
Single print is a volume between 1 and 9.

440
00:30:24,600 --> 00:30:27,000
A small print volume is more than 10.

441
00:30:28,900 --> 00:30:30,900
What is important is the ratio number.

442
00:30:31,300 --> 00:30:33,300
It indicates a lack of follow-through or

443
00:30:36,272 --> 00:30:39,272
you know, a lack of buying or a lack of selling.

444
00:30:39,972 --> 00:30:43,172
It's a reversal indicator in general.

445
00:30:43,872 --> 00:30:48,772
It's this one. It's called racial balance high. And this is the setting.

446
00:30:49,572 --> 00:30:51,872
I'll talk about it a bit more when I get to small prints.

447
00:30:54,272 --> 00:30:56,390
When I say ratio balance high, it's

448
00:30:56,390 --> 00:30:58,811
a level that I use to determine if

449
00:30:58,811 --> 00:31:00,929
there's going to be a lack of

450
00:31:00,929 --> 00:31:05,469
buying follow-through on a move up or a lack of selling on a move down.

451
00:31:07,472 --> 00:31:14,372
A ratio bounds low is what I use to determine if there's a large print occurring in a bar.

452
00:31:14,872 --> 00:31:17,735
I have my ratio bounds low set at 0.699 because

453
00:31:17,735 --> 00:31:20,280
I want to be notified when there's a

454
00:31:20,280 --> 00:31:24,734
ratio below 0.6999, which indicates there's a large print at the edge of a bar.

455
00:31:25,672 --> 00:31:28,372
So if it's at the bottom of a bar,

456
00:31:29,572 --> 00:31:34,972
that green, it'll be an indication of strong buying at the bottom of the bar.

457
00:31:34,972 --> 00:31:41,542
If it appears at the top of a red bar, it indicates strong offers up at the top of the

458
00:31:41,542 --> 00:31:41,871
bar.

459
00:31:42,872 --> 00:31:49,272
Again, I'll talk about the... Well, I did talk about the ratios of the large print earlier.

460
00:31:49,972 --> 00:31:52,472
And this is what the setting is. It's the ratio bounds low.

461
00:31:52,572 --> 00:31:57,972
Again, it's something that's only available in the OrderFlows trader software.

462
00:32:02,552 --> 00:32:05,700
Selling imbalance occurs when sellers are aggressively selling into the

463
00:32:05,700 --> 00:32:07,904
bid at a ratio of 400% or greater

